The dominant circuit is a feed-forward addition pathway: operator/task cues support operand integration, which branches into a main sum-magnitude representation and an auxiliary digit-control pathway. These converge on positive representations of the leading “1” and its final logit readout. Ablations support the causal importance of operand integration (13.7% relative drop) and the layer-32 sum representation (6.5% drop); mixed late-layer groups were excluded where their net effect was inhibitory.

