Ablations separate two necessary inputs: early Munich encoding caused a 58% relative drop, while the capital-relation/integration branch nearly eliminated Berlin. The strongest downstream mediator was the layer-30 relational evidence stream (85% drop); later auxiliary branches were largely redundant.

