Ablations isolate a strong capital-retrieval pathway: removing the capital-query/L27 features reduced Beijing from 0.937 to 0.00046, and removing the L28–30 answer route reduced it to 0.073. In contrast, ablating the Shanghai identity stream increased Beijing probability, indicating a competing copy-subject pathway rather than part of the supportive Beijing circuit.

